{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14603 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Pyrimethamine is implicated in the target relationship with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that pyrimethamine acts as a target for multiple entities, including SF-188, Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, and RXF 631, all of which are themselves targets of other compounds. These intermediates ultimately share a common target, (1R,4aR,4bS,7R,10aS)-7-ethenyl-1,4a,7-trimethyl-3,4,4b,5,6,9,10,10a-octahydro-2H-phenanthrene-1-carboxylic acid, which in turn has Replicase polyprotein 1ab as its target. This suggests a potential mechanism where pyrimethamine may influence the activity of these intermediates, which then modulate the replicase polyprotein 1ab. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for pyrimethamine in regulating replicase activity through a complex network of targets.",
